# Populate the map with vehicles and pedestrians.
#
# `near_ned` concentrates them: without it, spawn points are shuffled map-wide and a small
# fleet spreads across the whole of Town10HD, so a scenario that wanted busy streets gets an
# empty one. Measured on Town10HD: of 155 map-wide spawn points only ~45 lie within 60 m of
# the cross_the_plaza start.
int32 vehicles
int32 walkers
# UNBOUNDED on purpose. `float64[3]` is a FIXED-size array: it is always length 3, so
# "empty means map-wide" becomes unreachable, an unset request silently means the NED origin
# (which is offshore on Town10HD), and assigning [] serialises to uninitialised memory rather
# than erroring. Length 0 has to be expressible, and [0,0,0] is a real coordinate so it
# cannot double as the sentinel.
float64[] near_ned              # 3 values to concentrate around; EMPTY for map-wide
float64 radius_m                # <= 0 uses the sidecar default
---
bool success
int32 spawned                   # vehicles actually created - the map may refuse some
int32 walkers_spawned
string message
